I love psychological horror without jumpscares, so in that sense, this game was right up my alley. The puzzles aren't all that difficult, so Fingerbones is a cool way to pass 30 minutes. As a game, I liked it, and would've enjoyed playing more of it.
But what comes to the story, I'm not so sure. Some dude as a bitter megalomaniac who abandons the "constricting" moral rules of our society to torture a girl (and there was what sounded like hints of incest) isn't exactly groundbreaking, nor something I enjoy. Horror that is derived from girls or women getting tormented is lazy, misogynistic, and what makes me not recommend this game.
If you want to play it, why not, but the easy puzzles aren't really worth having to put up with incestuous torture p*rn.

