As someone who hasn't really given MMOs a fair shot as a genre due to not having a huge interest in it from the get-go and being a bit skeptical of pay subscription models, I am very glad that I was talked into picking this up by a friend. It is by far one of the most enjoyable games I have ever played, and having only picked up the game last week (at time of writing), the 27.8 hours that I already have logged in should be considered as a good indicator of just how enjoyable this game is, and how easy it is to be entralled in the universe that is Final Fantasy XIV: A Realm Reborn.
Due to my inexperience with the genre, perhaps I lack the keen eye to be able to spot what makes an MMO truly great. But as a newcomer to the genre, and perhaps yourself too being on the fence on whether to try this MMO out, hopefully my words are relatable and equally as helpful as those who are veteran MMO players:
Pros:
- Stunning visuals;
- Class Fluidity (being able to change classes on the fly; not having to worry about being pidgeon-holed into a class forever);
- Many classes and subclasses to choose from; variety ranging from combat, magic, trades, and artisan roles;
- Engaging storyline;
- Free 30-Days game time for newcomers;
- Very healthy population for a game that is already 3 years old;
- New content, patches and expansions still being released by developers (new expansion coming in 2017 for e.g.)
- Good guild support (in the game they are known as 'Free Companies');
- Party System to play with friends;
- Support for both Mouse and Keyboard, and Gamepad play;
- Player-run economies (nice bit of micro-economics between players if they wish to use their classes to develop products/ items and sell to others in order to make a bit of money. Also makes for good banter between friends);
- Nice balance of PvE and PvP content - you can quite easily enjoy both or pick one or the other if that's what you prefer.
Cons:
- Voice acting is a little lacking but otherwise great; there will be times often enough where you are just reading lines of text which can be a bit boring and/or skippingly tedious;
- Game is arguably and substantially more enjoyable with friends than it is without.

